OL,3,GNEWSAThefts from woman with Alzheimer's
OL,4,Adevastate family                       
OL,6,FThe family of a woman who had early    
OL,7,Fonset Alzheimer's when her partner     
OL,8,Fstole thousands of pounds from her have
OL,9,Fsaid his crimes have "devastated" their
OL,10,Ffamily.                                
OL,12,FDavid Brinded, 62, of Eaton, Norwich,  
OL,13,Fwas sentenced to 32 months in prison   
OL,14,Ffor fraud by abuse of position at      
OL,15,FNorwich Crown Court on Wednesday, after
OL,16,Fhe was found to have taken #21,500 from
OL,17,FRosalind Jeczalik to fund his          
OL,18,Flifestyle.                             
OL,23,APub: 27-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
